Chapter: SketchOnScreen
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Game chapter Rasterizer
  cites Game chapter Sprite
  cites Game chapter Color
  cites Game chapter Bresenham
  cites Math chapter Geometry
  cites Math chapter Quaternion

 What codex/test/rasterizer-test and codex/test/sprite-test draw, at a size
 worth seeing: Rasterizer's lines, rectangle, filled circle and triangle, and
 Sprite's keyed blit, horizontal flip and two-frame animation, all into one 80
 by 60 Framebuf, copied onto the screen that UEFI's GOP protocol describes
 with each of its pixels a block of the screen's. The arrows cross and the
 face blinks by the clock the framebuffer platform writes before each frame.

 We say:

Section: Screen

  fb-base : Integer = 3204448256
  cell-width : Integer = 1988
  cell-height : Integer = 1992
  cell-stride : Integer = 2016
  cell-clock : Integer = 2032

  sketch-w : Integer = 80
  sketch-h : Integer = 60

  paper : Integer = #1B1F2A
  gold : Integer = #F2C14E
  teal : Integer = #3FB6A8
  coral : Integer = #F26D5B
  lilac : Integer = #9D8DF1
  chalk : Integer = #F4F1E8

Section: Sprites

 Every sprite here is blitted keyed on 0, so its zero pixels show what lies
 beneath.

  arrow : Sprite
  arrow = sprite-from-pixels 7 5 [
    0, 0, 0, 0, chalk, 0, 0,
    0, 0, 0, 0, chalk, chalk, 0,
    chalk, chalk, chalk, chalk, chalk, chalk, chalk,
    0, 0, 0, 0, chalk, chalk, 0,
    0, 0, 0, 0, chalk, 0, 0
  ]

  face-open : Sprite
  face-open = sprite-from-pixels 6 6 [
    0, gold, gold, gold, gold, 0,
    gold, gold, gold, gold, gold, gold,
    gold, paper, gold, gold, paper, gold,
    gold, gold, gold, gold, gold, gold,
    gold, paper, paper, paper, paper, gold,
    0, gold, gold, gold, gold, 0
  ]

  face-shut : Sprite
  face-shut = sprite-from-pixels 6 6 [
    0, gold, gold, gold, gold, 0,
    gold, gold, gold, gold, gold, gold,
    gold, gold, gold, gold, gold, gold,
    gold, paper, gold, gold, paper, gold,
    gold, paper, paper, paper, paper, gold,
    0, gold, gold, gold, gold, 0
  ]

 The face stays open for 900 milliseconds and shut for 150, and loops.

  blink : SpriteAnim
  blink = anim-new [anim-frame 900 face-open, anim-frame 150 face-shut] True

Section: Sketch

  sketch-at : Integer -> Framebuf
  sketch-at (t) =
    let bg = fb-new sketch-w sketch-h paper
    in let l1 = fb-line bg 2 2 77 57 teal
    in let l2 = fb-line l1 2 57 77 2 teal
    in let r1 = fb-rect l2 4 4 20 14 lilac
    in let c1 = fb-circle-filled r1 62 15 10 coral
    in let t1 = fb-tri c1 40 20 24 50 56 50 lilac
    in let x = 2 + (t / 60) - ((t / 60) / 70) * 70
    in let s1 = sprite-blit-keyed t1 arrow x 52 0
    in let s2 = sprite-blit-keyed s1 (sprite-flip-h arrow) (72 - x) 2 0
    in let face = anim-current-sprite (spr-anim-tick blink (t - (t / 1050) * 1050))
    in sprite-blit-keyed s2 face 37 34 0

Section: Copy

 Each screen pixel takes the sketch's pixel it falls in, so the sketch fills
 the screen whatever its size.

  copy-cols : Framebuf, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  copy-cols (src) (stride) (w) (h) (y) (x) =
    if x >= w then 0
    else let c = fb-get src (x * (src.fb-width) / w) (y * (src.fb-height) / h)
    in let p = poke-32 fb-base ((y * stride + x) * 4) c
    in copy-cols src stride w h y (x + 1)

  copy-rows : Framebuf, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  copy-rows (src) (stride) (w) (h) (y) =
    if y >= h then 0
    else let d = copy-cols src stride w h y 0
    in copy-rows src stride w h (y + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let w = peek-32 cell-width 0
    in let h = peek-32 cell-height 0
    in let stride = peek-32 cell-stride 0
    in let t = peek-32 cell-clock 0
    in let d = copy-rows (sketch-at t) stride w h 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("clock : " & show t & " ms")
    end
  end
